Vault
A small and lightweight command line launcher.
==============================================

It's just a hobby and a way to automate tedious and repetitive tasks.

Installation:
-------------
To install, run the following commands:

   $ git clone https://github.com/sakaki91/vault $HOME/.local/share/vault

If you don't have a local binaries folder, run this:

   $ mkdir -p $HOME/.local/bin
   $ ln -sf $HOME/.local/share/vault/vault $HOME/.local/bin/

this will create the directory and a shortcut to the vault, and then add it to your PATH:

   $ echo 'export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"' >> "$HOME"/.bashrc

or if you use zsh/fish, adapt it to your shell's .rc file.

* But why??
This allows you to call it using only "vault" in the terminal, but using your local binaries folder, without interfering with the system's root directories.


Updating:
---------
To update, simply run:

   $ cd $HOME/.local/share/vault
   $ git pull


Do you want to delete?
----------------------
Just delete the directory $HOME/.local/share/vault:

   $ rm -rf $HOME/.local/share/vault

The script does not generate configuration files outside of its own directory.
